  "id": "1c90bca5-7146-56ed-8f42-57f7a736c95a",
  "slug": "polish-sloppy-joes",
  "name": "Polish Sloppy Joes",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "This is a recipe from my Husband's grandmother. Even people that aren't crazy about sauerkraut have raved about them. For a Rueben twist, serve on a good rye roll with a slice of Swiss.",
  "cuisine": "Inspired",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Crumble the ground beef in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook and stir until no longer pink. Pour in the sauerkraut and chicken broth and add the green pepper, celery and onion. Simmer for at least 1 hour. Season with salt and pepper to taste and serve on a good hard roll or a semmel (Kaiser) roll."
    }
  ],
